     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled outpatient dose of 3,200 mg/day. The usual limit is 800 mg per dose, and most inpatient regimens stay at or below 2,400 mg/day. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Something else\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. If 1600 mg four times daily really is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
